  "description": "A parametric SERVICES CEILING on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A SPACE. Everything runs along the space's longest edge (Rotation turns the runs) across its bounding box less the inset: a painted soffit plate, oval ducts, a cable tray and pipes, all at stated gaps below the soffit.\n\nTHE OVAL IS BUILT FACE BY FACE, not from boxes. A quad prism only extrudes vertically, and a duct runs horizontally, so each duct is ductFacets side faces whose corners sit on the ellipse (w/2·cos a, h/2·sin a) in the (v, z) plane, plus two end caps — every facet of every duct in ONE table indexed by floor(i/N). Rectangular is the same table at four facets turned 45° and scaled by √2.\n\nDEFAULTS are the INFRA Reception review: all ducts oval (s28), services white and complete (s18, s29), soffit at an assumed 3.6 m.",
